data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — permit2@cc56ad0f\n_human-validated 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/permit2/gasless-approval.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-11, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: ethereum\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: permit2 @1 :: gasless-approval\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 13 quotes · 8 structural · 9 fork assertions against deployed bytecode, all green. (Banner and stamp changed in the SAME edit — see aave-v3, where this drifted twice.)\nproject_id: \"permit2\"       # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 1            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. Permit2 publishes no semver at all:\n                            #   it is one immutable deployment at a deterministic address, with\n                            #   no version in the contract, the repo or any manifest. `1` here\n                            #   means \"the only deployment that has ever existed\", NOT \"major 1\n                            #   of a series\". Stated because the axis already carries two\n                            #   meanings on `dynamic`, and this is a third.\nversion: \"cc56ad0f\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. The pinned commit's short SHA, because that is the\n                            #   only version identity this project has. See version_discriminator.\ntype: \"gasless-approval\"\n\n# The chain the integration flow was actually exercised on. ⚠ NOT the three in `deployments` —\n# see the banner. Deployment verified on three, flow run on one.\nchains: [ethereum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# One address on every chain. ⚠ The BYTECODE is not one bytecode — see mistake #3.#\n# ⚠ NAMED 2026-08-15 (F-4, protocol rule 9). Each chain previously mapped straight to a bare\n#   address, so the typed table produced a row with no contract name — \"(unnamed in recipe)\" —\n#   and the address could be served but not asked for. The name is NOT the author's: it is the\n#   contract name Sourcify reports for the verified source at that exact address on that exact\n#   chain, attested in sources.json. ⚠ NO ADDRESS CHANGED; only a name was added around it.\n# 🔴 THIS EDIT POSTDATES THE STAMP ABOVE and the stamp was not touched — this row needs a fresh\n#   curator run before launch. Every address here resolves to `Permit2` on every chain listed.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    Permit2: \"0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3\"\n  base:\n    Permit2: \"0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3\"\n  arbitrum:\n    Permit2: \"0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Extracted VERBATIM to test/permit2/recipe/ by extract-recipe.ts and COMPILED BY FOUNDRY there,\n# so \"the shipped example is broken\" is a build failure rather than a discovery (recipe #1, D-1).\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"permit2\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/interfaces/ISignatureTransfer.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── WorkingExample.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    interface ISignatureTransfer {\n        struct TokenPermissions { address token; uint256 amount; }\n        struct PermitTransferFrom { TokenPermissions permitted; uint256 nonce; uint256 deadline; }\n        struct SignatureTransferDetails { address to; uint256 requestedAmount; }\n\n        function permitTransferFrom(\n            PermitTransferFrom memory permit,\n            SignatureTransferDetails calldata transferDetails,\n            address owner,\n            bytes calldata signature\n        ) external;\n\n        function DOMAIN_SEPARATOR() external view returns (bytes32);\n        function nonceBitmap(address owner, uint256 wordPos) external view returns (uint256);\n    }\n\n    /// The EIP-712 digest a signer must produce. This is the half developers get wrong, so it\n    /// ships as code rather than as prose. Both type strings are byte-for-byte the ones in\n    /// Uniswap/permit2 @ cc56ad0f — reproducing them approximately produces a valid-looking\n    /// signature that recovers to the wrong address.\n    library Permit2Digest {\n        bytes32 internal constant TOKEN_PERMISSIONS_TYPEHASH =\n            keccak256(\"TokenPermissions(address token,uint256 amount)\");\n\n        bytes32 internal constant PERMIT_TRANSFER_FROM_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\n            \"PermitTransferFrom(TokenPermissions permitted,address spender,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)TokenPermissions(address token,uint256 amount)\"\n        );\n\n        /// @param spender THE CONTRACT THAT WILL CALL permitTransferFrom — Permit2 reads this\n        ///        from msg.sender, and it is NOT a field of PermitTransferFrom.\n        function structHash(\n            address token,\n            uint256 amount,\n            address spender,\n            uint256 nonce,\n            uint256 deadline\n        ) internal pure returns (bytes32) {\n            bytes32 tokenPermissions =\n                keccak256(abi.encode(TOKEN_PERMISSIONS_TYPEHASH, token, amount));\n            return keccak256(\n                abi.encode(PERMIT_TRANSFER_FROM_TYPEHASH, tokenPermissions, spender, nonce, deadline)\n            );\n        }\n\n        /// Scoped to ONE chain: domainSeparator commits to block.chainid. A signature does not\n        /// travel, even though the Permit2 address does. See common_mistakes #3.\n        function digest(bytes32 domainSeparator, bytes32 hashOfStruct)\n            internal\n            pure\n            returns (bytes32)\n        {\n            return keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", domainSeparator, hashOfStruct));\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// A minimal spender. The owner signs; THIS contract submits and pays the gas.\n    contract Permit2Spender {\n        ISignatureTransfer public constant PERMIT2 =\n            ISignatureTransfer(0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3);\n\n        /// The owner must ALREADY have sent `approve(PERMIT2, …)` to `token`. That transaction\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 35342 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:permit2@cc56ad0f::gasless-approval::body@5798\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/interfaces/ISignatureTransfer.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/libraries/PermitHash.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/SignatureTransfer.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/EIP712.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/src/AllowanceTransfer.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/tree/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219\n\n---\n\n### permit2@latest::AllowanceTransferTest::__contract__~7\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/AllowanceTransferTest.t.sol#L666-L694\n\n```\nbytes memory sig = getPermitBatchSignature(permit, fromPrivateKey, DOMAIN_SEPARATOR);\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::AllowanceTransferTest::setUp\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/AllowanceTransferTest.t.sol#L58-L85\n\n```\nfunction setUp() public {\n        permit2 = new Permit2();\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::AllowanceTransferTest::__contract__~6\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/AllowanceTransferTest.t.sol#L636-L665\n\n```\nassertEq(expiration, defaultExpiration);\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::DeployPermit2Test::permit2\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/utils/DeployPermit2.t.sol#L13-L43\n\n```\nPermit2 permit2;\naddress from;\nuint256 fromPrivateKey;\naddress address0 = address(0);\naddress address1 = address(2);\nuint160 defaultAmount = 10 ** 18;\nuint48 defaultNonce = 0;\nuint32 dirtyNonce = 1;\nuint48 defaultExpiration = uint48(block.timestamp + 5);\n+3 more units in this chunk\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::MockPermit2::__contract__\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/mocks/MockPermit2.sol#L8-L49\n\n```\ncontract MockPermit2 is Permit2 {\n    function doStore(address from, address token, address spender, uint256 word) public {\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::SignatureTransferTest::FULL_EXAMPLE_WITNESS_BATCH_TYPEHASH\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/SignatureTransfer.t.sol#L49-L94\n\n```\nbytes32 constant FULL_EXAMPLE_WITNESS_BATCH_TYPEHASH = keccak256(\nPermit2 permit2;\naddress from;\nuint256 fromPrivateKey;\nuint256 defaultAmount = 1 ** 18;\naddress address0 = address(0x0);\naddress address2 = address(0x2);\nbytes32 DOMAIN_SEPARATOR;\nfunction setUp() public\n+2 more units in this chunk\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::AllowanceUnitTest::testUpdateAllRandomly\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/AllowanceUnitTest.sol#L36-L71\n\n```\nfunction testUpdateAllRandomly(uint160 amount, uint48 expiration, uint48 nonce) public\nfunction testPackAndUnpack(uint160 amount, uint48 expiration, uint48 nonce) public\n(2 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::Spender::__contract__\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/actors/Spender.sol#L7-L22\n\n```\ncontract Spender is Test {\n    Permit2 private immutable permit2;\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::NonceBitmapTest::permit2\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/NonceBitmap.t.sol#L10-L48\n\n```\nMockPermit2 permit2;\nfunction setUp() public\nfunction testLowNonces() public\nfunction testNonceWordBoundary() public\nfunction testHighNonces() public\n(5 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### permit2@latest::Permit2LibTest::testSimplePermit2PlusTransferFrom2WithNonPermit\n`permit2@latest` · repo:cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219 · as_of 2023-09-29T15:36:13Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/blob/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219/test/Permit2Lib.t.sol#L576-L616\n\n```\nfunction testSimplePermit2PlusTransferFrom2WithNonPermit() public\nfunction testPermit2DSLessToken() public\nfunction testPermit2DSMoreToken() public\nfunction testPermit2DSMore32Token() public\n(4 units in this chunk)\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"permit2","version":"cc56ad0f","recipe_type":"gasless-approval","last_validated":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.","gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: permit2 @1 :: gasless-approval\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 13 quotes · 8 structural · 9 fork assertions against deployed bytecode, all green. (Banner and stamp changed in the SAME edit — see aave-v3, where this drifted twice.)\nproject_id: \"permit2\"       # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 1            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. Permit2 publishes no semver at all:\n                            #   it is one immutable deployment at a deterministic address, with\n                            #   no version in the contract, the repo or any manifest. `1` here\n                            #   means \"the only deployment that has ever existed\", NOT \"major 1\n                            #   of a series\". Stated because the axis already carries two\n                            #   meanings on `dynamic`, and this is a third.\nversion: \"cc56ad0f\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. The pinned commit's short SHA, because that is the\n                            #   only version identity this project has. See version_discriminator.\ntype: \"gasless-approval\"\n\n# The chain the integration flow was actually exercised on. ⚠ NOT the